From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:53:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Walk the activation range's entity slices by index

ActivationRange.activateChunkEntities visits every entity of every chunk in
range on every tick, through UnsafeList's iterator - which searches a pool for
one not in use and resets it, and stores a field on every hasNext(). A profile
put hasNext() and iterator() together at 2.09% of the server thread, all of it
reached from this one loop.

Nothing in the loop touches the slice; it only stamps activatedTick. An index
therefore sees exactly the elements the iterator saw, in the same order. Same
change as the goal selector's loops and the entity slice scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/ActivationRange.java b/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/ActivationRange.java
index e4e403b222dd03de6af98828f199c6ae5734220e..176d466f779c5d89e59a7f576f35d84812117044 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/ActivationRange.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/spigotmc/ActivationRange.java
@@ -174,8 +174,16 @@ public class ActivationRange
     {
         for ( List<Entity> slice : chunk.entitySlices )
         {
-            for ( Entity entity : slice )
+            // Athena - by index. UnsafeList.iterator() searches a pool for an iterator not in use
+            // and resets it, and the Itr it returns stores a field on every hasNext(); this walk
+            // covers every entity of every chunk in range on every tick, and a profile put
+            // hasNext() and iterator() together at 2.09% of the server thread, all of it here.
+            // Nothing in the loop touches the slice, so an index sees exactly what the iterator
+            // saw. Same trade as the goal selector and the entity slice scan.
+            for ( int idx = 0; idx < slice.size(); ++idx )
             {
+                Entity entity = slice.get( idx );
+
                 if ( MinecraftServer.currentTick > entity.activatedTick )
                 {
                     if ( entity.defaultActivationState )
